What is Structural Steel?
Structural steel is a category of steel specifically manufactured for use as a construction material to create structural shapes. These standardized profiles, defined by specific chemical compositions and mechanical properties as regulated in most industrialized nations, provides the essential framework for modern buildings, bridges, and industrial facilities. Its versatility allows for the creation of everything from skyscrapers to distribution centers, driven by its exceptional strength-to-weight ratio, durability, and design flexibility. The material's inherent recyclability aligns perfectly with the global push toward sustainable construction practices, further cementing its position as the material of choice for ambitious architectural projects and large-scale infrastructure.
